How do I interpret user needs and implement them into a program? How does creating “user stories” help with this?

Interpreting user needs and implementing them into a program is a crucial part of software development.  Understanding user needs involves active engagement with stakeholders and users, gathering comprehensive requirements, and transforming them into "user stories".  These "user stories" help with understanding and interpreting the customer's need because they provide clear guidance to the development team on what the user wants and what will meet the Acceptance Criteria of the user story.

How do I approach developing programs? What agile processes do I hope to incorporate into my future development work?

My approach to developing programs has changed significantly over the length of this course.  Too many times, I would previously take a long time to get started on the actual development of the software I was not able to produce a functional product by the deadline or I did not properly estimate the amount of time it would take me so I was not able to meet all of the requirements for the software in time.  I was also not very resilient to change as when stakeholders wanted to change the direction of the project, I was not able to adapt very easily and, at some points, needed to start the entire project over again to make sure I was able to align myself with the new direction.  In the future, I will spend more time gathering the requirements of the program beforehand so I know exactly what the user wants the program to look like or be able to do. Still, it will also help me in creating user stories for these requirements and be able to properly estimate the amount of time or effort each user story may require to complete.  I would use an estimation technique like "Story Points" to help me estimate the amount of work needed for each story.

What does it mean to be a good team member in software development?

An effective team member in software development demonstrates proficiency in both technical abilities and interpersonal skills. They excel in clear and concise communication, collaboration with other members of the team, and are strongly commitment to the team's goals.  Their technical expertise, flexibility ability to adapt to change, and dedication contribute to a positive and efficient working environment which can greatly enhance the project's success.
